# 0.5: a group whose members auto-layout puts on DIFFERENT ranks
# can enclose a non-member between them — the engine keeps members together
# within a rank only (group-aware rank assignment is engine-backlog item 32).
# Nothing is pinned, so the engine chose every position, and the separation
# pass finds no free room. The figure is refused, and the refusal now ends
# with the one line measured to clear it: a `rank` holding the group's
# members. Experimental because the hint is this engine's layout, not a
# conformance requirement.
figdown 0.5 block
flow left
group g0 "G0"
group g1 "G1"
node n0 "NNN" in=g0
node n1 "NNN" in=g0
node n2 "NNNNNNNNNNNNNN" in=g1
node n3 "NNNNNNNNNNNNNNNN" in=g1
node n4 "NNN" in=g0
node n5 "NNNNNNNNNNN"
node n6 "NNN"
edge n6 -- n4
edge n4 -- n3
edge n1 -- n3
edge n0 -- n4
edge n0 -- n6